			<Item class="Script" referent="RBX893">
				<Properties>
					<bool name="Disabled">false</bool>
					<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
					<string name="Name">ReadMe</string>
					<string name="Source">--[[
thanks for using NZ&apos;s Code door.
This door is pretty simple to use if you know how to copy, paste, and type 1-3
first exit this script and Open the &quot;KeyPad&quot; and look for the Script Named &quot;MasterScript&quot;
Then Look At The Very Top For Somthing Called &quot;Code&quot; See the numbers to the right?
Chage them to your code... Your done! Simple eh? This door is very useful for obsticals with codes.
By default the code right now is &quot;1234&quot;

***New Feture***
	  |Turn|
{A new door opening animation}
first exit this script and Open the &quot;KeyPad&quot; and look for the Script Named &quot;MasterScript&quot;
One there, look for something called &quot;Turn.&quot; if you want the turn animation On change it to &quot;true&quot;
if you don&apos;t want the animation on change it to &quot;false&quot;
(This Animation has no real value, But if you like it, it&apos;s fine. NZ recimends it &quot;false&quot;)
(The Button to automatically open the door will not follow the animation due to inside script refrence)

Have fun!

P.S. Just try to move it on its Axis, Dragging it could damage the door.

--NZ (NintendoZACHERY)
--]]</string>
					<bool name="archivable">true</bool>
				</Properties>
			</Item>
